sops.workflow:
1. User -> Transportation Planner;
2. Transportation Planner -> Accommodation Planner;
3. Accommodation Planner -> Restaurant Planner
   Accommodation Planner -> Attractions Planner (in parallel);
4. Restaurant Planner, Attractions Planner -> Final Plan Summarizer;
5. Final Plan Summarizer -> End.

Description:
First, the Transportation Planner determines transportation modes and daily locations while enforcing state-specific city requirements (exactly 2 distinct PA cities) and closed-loop structure. After validating all transportation details with required tools and confirming budget compliance, it passes the logistical framework to the Accommodation Planner. The Accommodation Planner then arranges lodging with strict minimum_stay validation against itinerary nights and budget re-validation before proceeding. Subsequently, Restaurant and Attractions Planners work in parallel: Restaurant Planner uses mandatory day-city mapping to assign meals with no repetition across days, while Attractions Planner selects free activities with city alignment. Both enforce budget re-validation after adjustments. Finally, the Summarizer integrates all validated components into a cohesive itinerary with final constraint verification.
